[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The data model

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[NARRATIVE]
UID: NAR-WHITEBOARD-VIEW-DATA-MODEL
TITLE: The data model
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
WIDGET: rows
STATEMENT: >>>
One row per ruling the view rests on: this plan's decisions and requirements first, then the four spec rulings of 2026-08-30 the plan sits under. A row's word is the node's own state on the day of the render, read off the node, not a verdict of this page.

- A view is a tree of narratives: rows inside a statement, Cites for what a narrative presents, Contains for its parts in relation order. [LINK: DEC-NARRATIVE-IS-THE-VIEW-NODE] [ACCEPTED]
- The words a row may carry, with their colours and meanings, are rows of a legend narrative under the root, never a grammar field and never something the renderer knows. [LINK: DEC-LEGEND-IS-DATA] [ACCEPTED]
- Each ruled term is a narrative in the spec that cites its ruling, and a narrative that uses the term cites it, so retitling the term dirties every narrative that used it. [LINK: DEC-TERMS-ARE-NARRATIVES] [ACCEPTED]
- Whether code samples, diagrams and other maintained projections become types of their own or stay narratives with a widget. [LINK: DEC-INLINE-CODE-TYPE] [OPEN]
- What DEPTH means on a WORK node: design maturity, delivery, or nothing once execution state lives elsewhere. [LINK: DEC-WORK-STATE-FIELD] [OPEN]
- The renderer knows the shape of a payload and the widget words, never a UID, a type name or a plan. [LINK: REQ-VIEW-RENDERER-IS-CONTENT-BLIND] [ACCEPTED]
- No node outside the representation family carries a Parent relation or a fingerprint entry to a narrative. [LINK: REQ-NOTHING-DEPENDS-ON-A-NARRATIVE] [ACCEPTED]
- Node types come in four families, and only the definition grid is a grid; a narrative is the representation family. [LINK: DEC-NODE-FAMILIES] [ACCEPTED]
- A UID never changes: a retype changes the element tag, and the prefix names the type a node was born with. [LINK: DEC-UID-OUTLIVES-TYPE] [ACCEPTED]
- A rendered view is a regenerable deliverable computed from the export, never hand-edited and never the source. [LINK: DEC-VIEWS-ARE-REGENERABLE] [ACCEPTED]
- The node-type migration proceeds now, with WORK as a type, without waiting for beads. [LINK: DEC-MIGRATE-BEFORE-BEADS] [ACCEPTED]
<<<
PARENT_FP: >>>
DEC-INLINE-CODE-TYPE:0000000
DEC-LEGEND-IS-DATA:0000000
DEC-MIGRATE-BEFORE-BEADS:0000000
